{"html":"<p>The analytical stack has been quietly rewritten. The engine is Rust, the memory\nformat is Arrow, and the query language is still SQL.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-domain-demands\">What the domain demands</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Requirement</th>\n<th>Consequence</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Columnar memory</td>\n<td>Analytical scans touch 3 columns of 300; row layout wastes 99% of the I/O</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vectorised execution</td>\n<td>Process 1024 values per branch, not one</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-threaded by default</td>\n<td>A single-core dataframe library is a toy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Predictable memory</td>\n<td>OOM is the default failure mode of data work</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Interop</td>\n<td>Python, Java, R all need to read the same buffers without copying</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Arrow is the answer to the last one: a language-agnostic columnar memory layout\nwith zero-copy reads across FFI. Rust implementations of Arrow became the fastest\nones, and the engines followed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"who-runs-it\">Who runs it</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Project</th>\n<th>What it is</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Polars</strong></td>\n<td>a dataframe library with a lazy query optimiser, written in Rust, exposed to Python</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>InfluxDB IOx</strong></td>\n<td>InfluxDB 3's storage engine: Rust + Arrow + DataFusion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DataFusion</strong></td>\n<td>a query planner and execution engine you embed in your own product</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Materialize</strong></td>\n<td>streaming SQL over changing data, in Rust</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Databend, RisingWave</strong></td>\n<td>warehouse and stream-processing engines built on the same stack</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Delta-rs, iceberg-rust</strong></td>\n<td>table formats implemented in Rust for other engines to use</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The strategic shift: these are not Python tools with a Rust core. They are Rust\nengines with a Python binding, because the engine was the bottleneck.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-shape-of-the-code\">The shape of the code</h2>\n<p>A pipeline that reads 40 GB of Parquet without loading it:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> polars</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">prelude</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::*</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"> </span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">fn</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\"> daily_revenue</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(path</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> &#x26;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">str</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">-></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> PolarsResult</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">DataFrame</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">> {</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">    LazyFrame</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-d